The attached image illustrates Nano-11's role in improving antigen targeting to immunopotentiating cells and enhancing antigen retention at the injection site. Panel **a** shows that migratory dendritic cells (MigDCs) express the highest levels of CD86 among antigen-presenting cells in the draining lymph node. Panel **b** further details the phenotyping of OVA+ and OVA- MigDCs. Panel **c** demonstrates via in vivo imaging that Nano-11, similar to aluminum hydroxide (AH), significantly prolongs the retention of fluorescently labeled OVA at the injection site compared to soluble OVA, which rapidly clears. This sustained retention supports enhanced antigen delivery to the draining lymph node.